    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW266b2wAzfAJMBjD5JpGuLWE)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent; builds on #517 (already merged). Only `devonthink.lua` changes.\n\n## What changes\n\n- `Cmd+X` in DEVONthink toggles between the selection tool and the highlight tool.\n- It acts only when a PDF is shown. The test is that Tools > Annotate > Highlight Text exists and is enabled. Otherwise Cut is passed through unchanged.\n- It reads the real mode, so it is not blind: highlighting is on when the Highlight Text menu item has a check mark.\n  - On: it chooses the selection tool, an item in Tools > Annotate starting with Select, Pointer or Text Selection. If there is none, it chooses Highlight Text again to switch it off.\n  - Off: it chooses Highlight Text.\n  - If the menu shows no check marks at all, it falls back to the last state the key set. That is only a record of the last press and can be wrong if you switch tools with the mouse.\n- An alert shows \"Highlight\" or \"Select\" after each press.\n- `Caps+x` now uses the same toggle (before it only started highlighting). Keeping it as well makes sense: it is the key that works in every DEVONthink context and is the only one that shows an alert when no PDF is shown.\n- The colour keys still start highlighting, as before.\n\n## What is lost\n\n- Cut with `Cmd+X` stops working while a PDF is shown in DEVONthink, even in a text field of that window, such as an annotation note.\n- Text editors, the item list, rename fields and other apps still get Cut, because no PDF is shown there or the key is only active in DEVONthink.\n- The `Cmd+X` check reads the Annotate menu on each press, like `Cmd+Z`, so there may be a small delay.\n\n## Could not verify (no Mac or DEVONthink here)\n\n- The exact menu text: \"Highlight Text\", and the name of the selection tool, if there is one.\n- Whether DEVONthink puts a check mark on the active annotation tool.\n- Whether choosing Highlight Text again switches highlighting off.\n- Run `DEVONthink.dumpMenu(\"Tools\")` with a PDF open, once with highlighting on and once off, and send me the Annotate part if the toggle does the wrong thing.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Reload Hammerspoon: no error in the console.\n- [ ] Open a PDF in DEVONthink, press Cmd+X: the alert says \"Highlight\" and you can highlight text.\n- [ ] Press Cmd+X again: the alert says \"Select\" and you are back to the selection tool.\n- [ ] Switch tools with the mouse, then press Cmd+X: it still does the right thing (or tell me if it is wrong).\n- [ ] Caps+x gives the same toggle. With no PDF shown, it alerts \"No PDF shown\".\n- [ ] Select text in a rich-text or Markdown document and press Cmd+X: it cuts as usual.\n- [ ] In the item list and in a rename field, Cmd+X behaves as before.\n- [ ] Other apps: Cmd+X still cuts.\n- [ ] Cmd+Z, Cmd+Shift+Z and the colour keys still work.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCTb5QFPFZUd9wzRgq)_",
